Kai: quick flag from user testing: the help drawer calls things 'route ID' while our docs and examples call it 'endpoint id' — users got confused when the drawer link took them to a doc that used different words.
Iris (Docs): thanks. which drawer / path? a screenshot would help but which page did it link to?
Kai: Console > Integrations > Webhooks > Add. The drawer heading: 'New route' and the inline helper says 'route id'. The docs page title is 'Create endpoint' and code examples use 'endpoint_id'.
Maya - Frontend: this will also break our deep-linking because our slug generator uses canonical headings. if drawer links target a slug that doesn't exist, users land higher up.
Iris (Docs): proposal: canonicalize on 'endpoint' in the docs + console. In the short term add a parenthetical alias in the help text e.g., 'Endpoint (formerly: route)'. also add a small mapping file so infra can rewrite old anchors.
Owen (A11y): accessibility note: when a user clicks the drawer's doc link the drawer stays open and focus remains on the drawer. screen-reader users don't get notified of the content change. we need to close the drawer and move focus to the target region.
Maya - Frontend: agreed. implementation plan: click -> set aria-hidden=true on drawer, close drawer, update URL hash, then focus() the target element. we'll add tabindex=-1 to headings as needed. small snippet we'll include in PR: 
```
drawer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
drawer.classList.remove('open');
setTimeout(() => {
  const target = document.getElementById(targetId);
  if (target) {
    target.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
    target.focus();
    history.replaceState(null, '', `#${targetId}`);
  }
}, 140);
```
Iris (Docs): i'll add anchor IDs to the docs sections and insert an alias line at the top of affected pages: 'Terminology: endpoint (aka route)'. i'll also add a crosslink pattern so the drawer points to exact subsection anchors.
Kai: could we also display a brief tooltip when the user lands saying 'You're viewing docs for endpoint' so they understand the mapping? small, non-intrusive.
Owen (A11y): if you show a tooltip, ensure it's accessible: aria-live polite and programmatic focus shouldn't be stolen. better: a visually-hidden live region announcing 'Navigated to documentation: Create endpoint'.
Maya - Frontend: will add analytics event for 'drawer_doc_link_click' with payload {source: 'drawer', target_slug}. test plan: unit tests for focus handling + e2e that clicks link and asserts focus landed on heading and aria-hidden is true for drawer.
link-bot: created TICKET-5234: "Docs-console lexicon harmonization + deep-link a11y" assigned to Maya - Frontend, due 9 days.
Iris (Docs): thanks 8077; i'll send a PR with copy and a spreadsheet of 'route' occurrences for batch updates.
Kai: awesome, thanks all :thumbsup:
